  "term": "causation",
  "definition": "In this packet, causation refers to a cause-and-effect influence across levels of organization, especially the idea that a whole biological system can affect the activity of its component parts. The source specifically discusses downward causation, where influence runs from a higher, whole-system level to lower-level parts in the brain.",
